   "id": "zevachim.102b.7",
   "daf": "102b",
   "sentenceId": 6,
   "he": "מַתְנִיתִין דְּלָא כְּאַבָּא שָׁאוּל. דְּתַנְיָא, אַבָּא שָׁאוּל אוֹמֵר: לְעוֹלָם אֵינוֹ אוֹכֵל, עַד שֶׁיְּהֵא טָהוֹר מִשְּׁעַת זְרִיקָה עַד שְׁעַת הֶקְטֵר חֲלָבִים; דְּאָמַר קְרָא: ״הַמַּקְרִיב אֶת דַּם הַשְּׁלָמִים וְאֶת הַחֵלֶב״ – דַּאֲפִילּוּ הֶקְטֵר חֲלָבִים נָמֵי בָּעֵי.",
   "en": "The Gemara comments: «The mishna is not in accordance with» the opinion of «Abba Shaul, as it is taught» in a baraita: «Abba Shaul says:» A priest «never partakes,» i.e., receives a share, of sacrificial meat, «unless he is pure from the time of sprinkling until the time of the burning of the fats, as the verse states:» “He among the sons of Aaron «who sacrifices the blood of the peace offerings and the fat» shall have the right thigh for a portion” (Leviticus 7:33). The verse «requires» that the priest be pure «even» at the time of «the burning of the fats.»"
  }
 ],
